CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ forwarding-ref accepts a const enum lvalue: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG: must fail: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^found no match for symbol 'pass'$
--
N5008 [temp.deduct.call]/3 + [dcl.enum]/[basic.type.qualifier]: a forwarding
reference `T&&` deduces T as "lvalue reference to A" from an lvalue argument of
type A, for any A including an enumeration; a const enum argument gives a
`const E&` parameter.  CBMC used to reject this ("found no match" -> CONVERSION
ERROR) for a const enum argument only: the deduced `const E&` parameter had its
const dropped by cpp_convert_plain_type, which (unlike for struct_tag/union_tag)
routed a `c_enum_tag` through the general conversion path that rebuilds the type
and loses cv-qualifiers, so the deduced parameter became a non-const `E&` that a
const enum lvalue could not bind.  Fixed by treating `c_enum_tag` as a tag
reference (left untouched, preserving cv) like `struct_tag`/`union_tag`.
Reduced (via cvise keeping real headers) from src/util/validate_expressions.cpp
`call_on_expr<...>(ns, vm)`, which forwards a `const validation_modet`
(enum class).  assertion.2 provides non-vacuity.
